<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    PaylisherATT — privacy manifest for the OPTIONAL advertising-identifier add-on.

    This manifest applies ONLY to apps that deliberately link the PaylisherATT module. Apps
    using the core Paylisher SDK alone never see it, and never inherit the tracking
    declaration below, because Xcode aggregates only the manifests actually present in the
    built app.

    If you link this module you are declaring that your app tracks. That has consequences you
    must accept up front:
      - Your App Store privacy nutrition label must declare "Data Used to Track You".
      - Your app MUST present the ATT prompt. Declaring tracking without a visible
        permission request is the single most common ATT rejection (Guideline 2.1). Call
        PaylisherATT.requestAuthorization(_:) from your own onboarding.
      - Info.plist MUST contain NSUserTrackingUsageDescription.

    ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    NSPrivacyTrackingDomains — WHY IT IS A SEPARATE HOSTNAME
    ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    Two Apple rules pull in opposite directions:
      - NSPrivacyTracking=true REQUIRES at least one entry here. Apple's own documentation:
        "When set to true you need to provide a list of internet domains in
        NSPrivacyTrackingDomains." App Store Connect enforces it at upload as ITMS-91064
        "Invalid tracking information", and it validates third-party SDK manifests too, so
        an add-on that declares tracking with no domain simply cannot be shipped.
      - iOS 17 and later FAIL every network request to a domain listed here whenever ATT is
        not authorized.

    So the domain listed here must carry ONLY identifier-bearing traffic. It deliberately is
    NOT link.paylisher.com: that host also serves the non-identifying fingerprint lookup, and
    listing it would break deferred deep linking for every user who was never prompted, every
    user who declined, the Simulator, and any customer who chooses never to prompt at all.

    That is Apple's prescribed hostname separation ("host tracking functionality at
    tracking.example.com, and non-tracking functionality at non-tracking.example.com"), and
    it is what every MMP does: att.attr.appsflyersdk.com, api-safetrack.branch.io,
    safetrack.singular.net.

    The SDK enforces the split in code: PaylisherDeferredDeepLinkAPI swaps the request host to
    PaylisherDeferredDeepLinkConfig.attTrackingHost when — and only when — an IDFA is attached,
    and drops the IDFA entirely if that host is unset. Fingerprint-only traffic never reaches
    this domain, so the iOS 17 block cannot affect it.

    ⚠️ DEPLOYMENT PREREQUISITE: att.link.paylisher.com must resolve and serve the
    deferred-deeplink endpoint before this module is published. The value below and
    PaylisherDeferredDeepLinkConfig.attTrackingHost must stay identical. The CORE SDK is
    unaffected either way — it never contacts this host.

    Format rules from TN3181: hostname only - no scheme, no path, no trailing slash.
-->

<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<true/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array>
		<string>att.link.paylisher.com</string>
	</array>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array>
		<!--
		    The IDFA (ASIdentifierManager.advertisingIdentifier), read only after the user
		    grants ATT authorization, and used to attribute an install to the ad click that
		    produced it.
		-->
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeDeviceID</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeThirdPartyAdvertising</string>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAnalytics</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array/>
</dict>
</plist>
